    "body": "Thank you for the issue — this is a real gap, and one that quietly corrupts the graph rather than failing loudly, which makes it worth more than its size suggests.\n\nTracked by **#378**, which is open with review comments and currently conflicting with `main`. It carries `Fixes #377`, so this will close automatically when that lands.\n\nThe approach is right (compare the previous patch manifest, emit explicit deletions, track dependents so a recreated file heals its callers). The blocking item on the PR is that `reconcileRemovedEntities` runs before `stripMapModeOps`, which means `ix map` after `ix ingest` deletes chunk nodes it never recreates — reproduced on the branch. Detail on the PR.\n",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/ix-infrastructure/Ix/issues/377#issuecomment-5245018777",
